---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const NUMBERS = [
  { num: '2019', label: 'first tee printed' },
  { num: '14k', label: 'orders shipped' },
  { num: '3', label: 'people in the team' },
  { num: '1', label: 'small warehouse' },
];
---

<Layout title="About — njX Shop" description="Who makes njX Shop: three people, one warehouse, goods for the hours nobody sees.">
  <section class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-10 px-5 pb-4 sm:pb-8 pt-6 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_1fr] md:pt-12">
    <div>
      <img src="/logo/njx-shop-dark.png" alt="njX Shop logo" class="logo-on-light mb-6 h-16 w-16 rounded-xl" />
      <img src="/logo/njx-shop-light.png" alt="njX Shop logo" class="logo-on-dark mb-6 h-16 w-16 rounded-xl" />
      <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(36px,5vw,60px)] font-extrabold leading-[1.02] tracking-tight">
        Built for the hours nobody sees.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-[52ch] text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        njX Shop started as a side table of leftover conference tees and one bag of
        over-roasted beans. It grew into a small catalog of things we actually use
        every day: clothes that survive the wash, wood that outlives the laptop on
        top of it, coffee that ships the week it's roasted.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[52ch] text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        We're three people and one warehouse. No growth team, no seasonal drops —
        a product joins the catalog when we've used it for a month and still like it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-tile">
      <img src="/products/hero.jpg" alt="The desk where njX Shop gets planned" class="aspect-[4/5] w-full object-cover" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5">
    <div class="grid gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-tile/60 p-4 text-center sm:grid-cols-4 sm:gap-8 sm:p-10">
      {NUMBERS.map((n) => (
        <div>
          <p class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-pine">{n.num}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-[14px] text-muted">{n.label}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="theme" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl scroll-mt-24 px-5 pt-4 sm:pt-8">
    <div class="grid gap-5 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-tile/60 p-4 sm:gap-10 sm:p-10 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <p class="text-[13px] font-medium text-pine">The honest part</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-[clamp(24px,3vw,32px)] font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight">
          This store is a demo. The theme is real.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The tees, the warehouse, Jamie and their hundred deploys — all invented to show
          <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">njx-store</strong>, a free ecommerce theme
          for Astro, working at full speed. This is the Lite version: fork it, swap the
          catalog, and you have a storefront of your own. An extended Pro version with more
          sections and pages is on the way.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/njbSaab/astro-njx-store" class="mt-6 inline-block rounded-md bg-pine px-6 py-3.5 text-[15px] font-semibold text-white hover:bg-pine-deep">
          Get it on GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-[16px] font-semibold">How the integration works</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-4 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="mt-1 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-pine"></span>
            <span><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Astro 5 renders everything statically.</strong> A Node.js build fetches the catalog once and ships pure HTML — no client framework, fast by default.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="mt-1 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-pine"></span>
            <span><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Two data providers, one switch.</strong> <code class="rounded bg-tile px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px]">COMMERCE_PROVIDER=mock</code> uses the bundled JSON catalog; <code class="rounded bg-tile px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px]">shopify</code> pulls real products over the Shopify Storefront API (GraphQL).</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="mt-1 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-pine"></span>
            <span><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Checkout stays on Shopify.</strong> The cart lives in localStorage; at checkout the theme creates a Shopify cart and hands off to their hosted, PCI-compliant checkout.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3">
            <span class="mt-1 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-pine"></span>
            <span><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Hosted on Cloudflare Pages.</strong> Static output deploys in seconds and runs comfortably on the free tier.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:py-14 text-center">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Want to say hi?</h2>
    <p class="text-[15px] text-muted">We answer every email ourselves — usually within a day.</p>
    <a href="/contacts" class="rounded-md bg-pine px-6 py-3.5 text-[15px] font-semibold text-white hover:bg-pine-deep">
      Contact us
    </a>
  </section>
</Layout>
